% Chapter 6
\chapter{Higgs Boson Production Cross Sections Dependence on Centre-of-Mass Energy}\label{Chapter6}
\chaptermark{Higgs boson production cross sections dependence on $\sqrt{s}$}
\section{Inclusive Fiducial Cross Section at $\sqrt{s}=13 \TeV$}
\subsection{Introduction}
After two year of long shutdown, the LHC Run II began to deliver data at enhanced center-of-mass energy of $\sqrt{s}=13 \TeV$. The Run II 
provide the opportunity of explore new era Higgs precision measurement including rediscovering, and studies of its rare production modes such as
as vector boson fusion (VBF) and associated production with a vector boson ($\WH$, $\ZH$) and with a top quark pair ($\ttH$). 
This chapters presents the  Higgs boson inclusive fiducial cross section measurement with $\Hllll$ decay channel at $\sqrt{s}=13$~TeV, using
$\usedLumi$ of proton-proton  collisions data recorded with the CMS  detector during the LHC Run in 2015.
\subsection{Datasets and Event Selection}
\subsubsection{Triggers and Datasets}
This measurements crossponds to 2.8~\ifb  at $\sqrt{s}=13$~TeV collected by CMS detector in 2015. All the datasets used for this analysis are 
summarized in Table~\ref{tab:datasets_data}. The online event selections is derived by single, double and triple leptons triggers. 
The trigger used in 2015 are summarized in Table~\ref{tab:triggerPaths}. The efficiencies of the triggers has been calculated based on single 
leptons trigger events and found to greater than 97\% for 4e and 2e2$\mu$ final state and and 99\% for $4\mu$.
