\subsection{Analysis Strategy}
 The fiducial phase space definition is consistent with Run I measurement described in Section~\ref{sec:FiducialVolume}. The only difference 
 with respect to Run I is that leptons are defined as "dressed `` leptons instead of ''born-level`` leptons. Dressed leptons are defined by 
 adding the four-momentum of all photons within cone of radius $\Delta R < 0.4$  around bare leptons.
 \par The background modeling and statistical procedure of maximizing likelihood and extraction of parameter of interest ($\sigma_{fid}$) is also 
 identical as described in Sections~\ref{sec:background_model} and~\ref{sec:SignalStatProcedure}.
 \par The Fiducial acceptance ($A_{fid}$), Fiducial efficiencies (reconstruction efficiency ($\epsilon$)) per final state  are extracted in
 similar way and listed in Tables~\ref{tab:acceptanceSM_Run2}~and~\ref{tab:efficiencySM_Run2}.
