The variation between different models of the factor in the final column of Table~\ref{tab:summarySM_Run2}, $(1+f_{\rm{nonfid}})\epsilon$, is directly
related to the model dependence of the measurement. The model dependence is defined as the variation of the factor
$(1+f_{\rm{nonfid}})\epsilon$ when the relative fraction of each the production modes are varied within there experimental constraints. The change
in the isolation working point (based on the studies in Sections \ref{sec:muoniso} and \ref{sec:eleiso} ) at reconstruction level in the current analysis increases the model dependence compared to the Run I analysis.
In order to reduce this model dependence the definition of the isolation at the fiducial level can be changed to match more closely the reconstruction
level. If the fiducial isolation definition is updated to use a cone size of 0.3 and a cut of 0.35 the difference 
of $~20\%$ between $\ggH$ and $\ttH$ in the factor $(1+f_{\rm{nonfid}})\epsilon$ in Table~\ref{tab:summarySM_Run2} is reduced to $2\%$.

