\subsubsection{Signal Shape Parameterization}
 \par The signal line shape is also parametrized as a function of $m(\rm{H})$ in the inclusive category to be used. This is accomplished by
performing a simultaneous fit of several mass points for $\ggH$ production around 125~\GeV. Each parameter of the double crystal ball 
function is set to be a linear function of $m(\rm{H})$ for a total of 12 free parameters. The correlation among these 12 parameters is 
checked and parameters are dropped to remove large correlations, or if the parameter is constant within the uncertainty. The resulting fits
after the final set of parameters is obtained are shown in Figures~\ref{fig:sigShapeSimFit120}-\ref{fig:sigShapeSimFit130}. The correlation
matrix is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:sigShapeSimFitCorrelation} and the $\chi^{2}/$ndof for each mass point is shown in 
Figure~\ref{fig:sigShapeSimFitChi2}
