\subsection{Results}
The result of the simultaneous fit to to the $\mllll$ spectrum is shown for each final state in Fig.~\ref{fig:fiducialfit}. The fiducial cross section
using this definition is measured to be:

\begin{eqnarray}
\label{eqn:fidresult}
\sigma_{{\rm fid.}}=2.48^{+1.45}_{-1.12}({\rm stat.})^{+0.28}_{-0.17}({\rm sys.})^{+0.01}_{-0.04}({\rm model~dep.})~{\rm fb}
\end{eqnarray}

This can be compared to the SM expectation $\sigma_{{\rm fid.}}^{\rm SM}=2.39~{\rm fb}$. The fiducial cross section measured using the updated
fiducial lepton isolation definition is measured to be $\sigma_{{\rm fid.}}=2.66^{+1.58}_{-1.22}~{\rm fb}$ with model dependence less
than $1\%$, and can be compared to the SM expectation of $\sigma_{{\rm fid.}}^{\rm SM}=2.50~{\rm fb}$.
