\section{Higgs Fiducial Cross Section Measurements vs. $\sqrt{s}$}
Figure \ref{fig:fiducialresult} shows the inclusive fiducial cross section as a function of $\sqrt{s}$ for 7, 8 and 13~TeV. The measurements are compared
with theoretical prediction based on SM calculations. The total uncertainties is represented by error bars can be splitted into statistical (black) and 
systematic (red), combined in quadrature. The model dependence is shown in grey box.  Theoretical predictions along with their uncertainties are shown in 
blue at the NNLL+NNLO accuracy. The acceptance are estimated at parton level using {\sc HRes} for the dominant $\ggH$ production mode, the hadronization
effects are been included by using {\sc Pythia 6.4}} and {\sc powheg+JHUgen}. 
\begin{figure}[!h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.75\linewidth]{Chapters/Chapter6_Figures/xs_vs_sqrts.pdf}
\caption{Higgs Fiducial cross section measurement as a function of $\sqrt{s}$}

\label{fig:fiducialresult}
\end{figure}
